        "title": "Introductory Note",
        "content": "Hey Champ! Welcome to **Module 17** of *Rupaiya 101*. If you have read the previous modules of this book, then by now you have understood the core fundamentals of budgeting (Module 2), banking (Module 6), escaping debt traps (Module 5), credit card strategies, and stock market investments (Module 7). But in 2026's digital India, just earning and investing money is not enough — **protecting your hard-earned money from fraud, staying safe from scam apps, and fully utilizing your consumer rights is equally crucial.**\n\nIn today's world, cybercriminals no longer offer simple phishing SMS or fake bank calls. Now they are using artificial intelligence, voice cloning, deepfakes, automated financial engineering, and high-tech psychological manipulation techniques. On the other side, modern fintech apps are targeting your brain's dopamine pathways to make you do impulse shopping, lose your entire semester's college fees in F&O options trading, or trap you in deceptive \"Buy Now Pay Later\" (BNPL) schemes that destroy your CIBIL score.",
