    "id": "17-5",
    "title": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS)",
    "emoji": "🔒",
    "color": "#10B981",
    "description": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS)",
    "cards": [
      {
        "id": "17-5-1",
        "topicId": "17-5",
        "topicTitle": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS)",
        "cardIndex": 1,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS)",
        "content": "When you face a financial dispute with a commercial bank, prepaid wallet company, or financial institution — such as unauthorized money fraud debit, failed UPI transaction where money was debited but no refund came, or a bank customer care issue that the bank refuses to resolve — then most college students feel helpless. They think *\"Bank people are massive corporations, who will listen to us simple students?\"*\n\nThis is a completely wrong belief! The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has the **RBI Integrated Ombudsman Scheme (RB-IOS)**, which holds strict statutory judicial authority over all banks and financial institutions in India.\n\n---\n\n### 17.3.1 RBI Integrated Ombudsman Scheme (RB-IOS)\n\n#### What is RB-IOS?\n**RB-IOS** (*\"One Nation, One Ombudsman\"*) is a free, statutory quasi-judicial grievance redressal mechanism established by the Reserve Bank of India. Its core objective is to resolve bank customers' and digital wallet users' complaints in a fast, cost-effective manner with strict binding enforcement.\n\n#### Entities Covered Under RBI Ombudsman (RB-IOS) Authority\n- All Commercial Banks (SBI, HDFC Bank, ICICI Bank, Axis Bank, Punjab National Bank, etc.)\n- Regional Rural Banks (RRBs) and Scheduled Primary Co-operative Banks\n- All RBI-registered Non-Banking Financial Companies (NBFCs)\n- Non-Bank Prepaid Payment Issuers (UPI Apps and Wallets: Paytm, PhonePe, Google Pay, Amazon Pay)\n- System Participants (Credit Bureaus: CIBIL, Experian, Equifax, CRIF High Mark)\n\n#### Valid Grounds for Filing Complaint Under RB-IOS\n1. Unauthorized electronic banking fraud transaction where the bank denies refund or credit.\n2. Failed ATM cash withdrawal or failed UPI payment where the account was debited but the payee did not receive and the bank did not auto-reverse within the specified time (T+1 days).\n3. Wrongful credit card charges levied, hidden fees deducted, or unauthorized annual fees charged.\n4. Non-disbursement or delay in sanctioned loan amount, educational loan processing, or insurance claim settlement.\n5. Discriminatory treatment, unfair practices, or deficiency in service by the regulated entity.",
        "color": "#10B981",
        "emoji": "🔒",
        "interactiveType": "no"
      },
      {
        "id": "17-5-2",
        "topicId": "17-5",
        "topicTitle": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS)",
        "cardIndex": 2,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS) (Part 2)",
        "content": "**Portal Web Link:** [https://cms.rbi.org.in](https://cms.rbi.org.in) \n**National Toll-Free Helpline Number:** **14448**\n\n```\n[Visit cms.rbi.org.in] ──> [OTP Mobile Verification] ──> [Select Regulated Entity] ──> [Upload Proof and Dispute Memo] ──> [Claim Compensation] ──> [Track Status]\n```\n\n#### Detailed Walkthrough of Online Complaint Process\n\n- **Step 1: Identity Registration and OTP Verification:**\n Open the website portal and click on *\"File a Complaint\"*. Enter your Full Name, active Mobile Number, and complete the OTP authentication.\n\n- **Step 2: Select Regulated Financial Entity:**\n From the drop-down listing menu, select the exact bank, NBFC, or UPI payment app name against which you want to lodge the grievance (for example, *State Bank of India* or *Paytm Payments Bank*).\n\n- **Step 3: Populate Incident and Financial Data:**\n - Exact Date and Time of the incident / fraudulent transaction.\n - Savings account number / UPI Reference UTR number / credit card number.\n - Total financial amount involved in the dispute (for example, Rs.22,500).\n - Categorization of Complaint (select: *\"Electronic Banking / Digital Transactions / Unauthorized Debit / Service Deficiency\"*).\n\n- **Step 4: Upload Mandatory Documentation (PDF format):\n - Copy of the initial written complaint/email submitted to the Bank's Grievance Redressal Officer (GRO).\n - Bank account statement PDF clearly highlighting the disputed debit entry.\n - Cyber Crime Complaint Acknowledgement receipt / FIR Copy (in case of fraud).\n - Bank's rejection letter/email screenshot (or proof that 30 calendar days have elapsed without resolution).\n\n- **Step 5: Specify Relief Claimed and Compensation Application:**\n Specify the exact monetary refund amount requested (disputed principal amount). Enter statutory compensation claims for mental harassment, delay trauma, or legal expenses.\n\n#### Compensation Limits Under RBI Ombudsman Scheme\n\n| Compensation Category | Maximum Limit |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Mental harassment and agony | Up to Rs.5,000 |\n| Financial loss not exceeding Rs.1 lakh | Up to Rs.1 lakh |\n| Financial loss exceeding Rs.1 lakh | Up to Rs.10 lakh |\n| Complaint not resolved within 30 days | Additional Rs.10,000 per delay |",
        "color": "#10B981",
        "emoji": "🔒",
        "interactiveType": "no"
      },
      {
        "id": "17-5-3",
        "topicId": "17-5",
        "topicTitle": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS)",
        "cardIndex": 3,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Consumer Rights and RBI Ombudsman Portal (CMS) (Part 3)",
        "content": "### 17.3.3 Zero Liability Policy of RBI for Unauthorized Electronic Transactions\n\n> **RBI Master Direction Reference:** DBR.No.Leg.BC.78/09.07.005/2017-18 (*Customer Protection — Limiting Liability of Customers in Unauthorized Electronic Banking Transactions*).\n\nEven if cyber fraud occurs, how much refund claim a student gets depends on **this critical fact — how quickly you report to the bank to formally notify them.** RBI law categorizes customer liability into 3 precise operational tiers:\n\n#### RBI Customer Liability and Refund Framework\n\n| Reporting Timeline to Bank Post Fraud Incident | Customer Financial Liability | Bank's Mandatory Refund Liability | Mandatory Credit SLA (Timeline) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Within 3 Working Days** | **ZERO customer liability (Rs.0 Loss)** | **100% Full Refund** by bank | Credit in bank account within **10 Working Days** |\n| **Between 4 to 7 Working Days** | **Limited Customer Liability** (Capped at Rs.10,000 for Savings Accounts / Rs.25,000 for Credit Cards) | Balance financial amount refunded by bank | Case resolution per Board approved policy (maximum 90 days) |\n| **Beyond 7 Working Days** | Subject to Bank's individual Board Discretionary policy | Subject to Bank's Internal Discretionary policy | No statutory guarantee timeline |\n| **Customer Contributory Negligence (shared OTP/PIN)** | **100% Full Customer Liability** (Unless reported before money leaves system or bank system breach) | **0% Refund** from bank | N/A |\n\n#### Key Strategic Lesson for Indian Students\nIf unauthorized money is debited from your account due to a cyber breach, SIM swap, or malware (without you sharing OTP/PIN), then **your absolute number 1 action priority is to inform the bank customer care and branch manager via email and phone within 24 hours.** Reporting within 3 working days = **100% Statutory Guarantee Refund!**",
        "color": "#10B981",
        "emoji": "🔒",
        "interactiveType": "no"
      }
    ]
