        "topicTitle": "Investor and Insurance Grievance Redressal",
        "cardIndex": 1,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Investor and Insurance Grievance Redressal",
        "content": "When a college student starts building assets and invests in equity/mutual funds (Cross-reference to Module 7: Investment Economics) or purchases personal health/vehicle insurance policies (Cross-reference to Module 9: Insurance Economics), conflicts can emerge with market brokers, depository participants, and insurance underwriting companies.\n\nFinancial loss from broker app glitches, Demat account getting frozen, or an insurance company arbitrarily rejecting a genuine medical hospitalization claim — in all these scenarios, regulatory statutory bodies have dedicated online escalation platforms.\n\n---\n\n### 17.4.1 SEBI SCORES 2.0 (Stock Market and Mutual Fund Disputes)\n\n#### What is SCORES 2.0?\n**SCORES** (*SEBI Complaints Redress System*) is a powerful, centralized online dispute redressal portal by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) where individual retail investors can register legal complaints against stock market intermediaries.\n\n#### Intermediaries Covered Under SEBI SCORES 2.0\n- **Stock Brokers and Trading Platforms:** Zerodha, Groww, Angel One, Upstox, ICICI Direct, HDFC Securities, etc.\n- **Depository Participants (DPs):** Central Depository Services Limited (CDSL), National Securities Depository Limited (NSDL).\n- **Mutual Fund Asset Management Companies (AMCs):** SBI Mutual Fund, HDFC AMC, Nippon India MF, Zerodha Fund House, etc.\n- **Registrar and Transfer Agents (RTAs):** CAMS, KFintech.\n- **SEBI Registered Investment Advisers (RIA) and Research Analysts (RA).**\n\n#### Common Student Investor Dispute Scenarios\n1. Trading app technical glitch causes a stop-loss order not to trigger and the client account suffers massive unwarranted loss.\n2. Stock buy order is executed, payment is debited, but purchased shares are not credited to the Demat account by T+1 settlement day.\n3. Stock broker levies unauthorized AMC (annual maintenance charges) or hidden brokerage fees.\n4. Mutual fund redemption amount is not credited within the stipulated NAV settlement timeline.",
